## Verification performed by the author

1. Freeze 2 focused source suite: 126 tests pass. Exact commands and exit codes are in freeze2-accepted-check-commands.json; raw output in freeze2-accepted-focused-tests.log. It covers actual SDK codec/portable integration, one-call behavior, generic failures, gap/LMT/local-noon context, early unsupported paths with zero natal calls, Blob cleanup, action surfaces and six-locale parity. Strict focused TypeScript succeeds. Astro check reports 1,038 files, zero errors, zero warnings and 11 existing hints.
2. Exact final receipt helper compatibility matrix: all 2,136 cases pass (356 city-index zones × UI date extremes 1800-01-01/2199-12-31 × known 00:00/23:59 and unknown 12:00), with actual legacy-chart comparison and SDK envelope parsing. See freeze2-accepted-compatibility-extremes-result.json and the command/subject/module-input artifacts. This tests current host compatibility, not an independent astronomical or historical oracle. Representative gap/fold/LMT/non-hour/skipped-day cases are also focused source controls.
3. Native interaction fixture: tests/interaction-replay-drive.mjs executes the actual bundled directive and real form controls in Chrome. Final 16 controls pass, including untouched shared initialization, explicit reset-to-default, eventless value changes representing autofill before module arrival or directive registration, newer edits during commit, replaced inputs, textarea, checkbox, normalized native defaults, single/multiple option reordering, load/hydrate retries and exactly one queued submit. See interaction-final/interaction-result.json for source/bundle hashes, requests, results and browser/server cleanup. Final correction strict TypeScript passes. The intermediate correction also passed Astro check; the final stable-value change was separately strict-typechecked and built.
4. Combined actual-site receipt flow: browser-1788847953353/result.json reports 12/12 groups pass, source hashes before/after, 1,359 requests and 123 served-file byte/hash identities. It records actual keyboard downloads in all six languages, sensitive generic filenames, existing wheel/share/save action presence, requested Placidus polar fallback, unknown local noon/no houses, replacement calculation, same-task stale DOM click suppression, fixed Blob-allocation error/retry with identical bytes, four unavailable input paths and positions-only exclusion. Ten JSON download files and desktop/mobile captures are retained. All recorded browser/console errors and external requests are empty. Blob URL creation/revocation, chart event counts and storage snapshots include observer negative controls. The event count is a UI observation, not proof of native natal call count; independent native precise-coverage checks are attributed to the reviewer. Every context, browser and static server was closed. This run served the raw successful Astro build plus the existing Guide asset build.
5. Existing Russian acceptance: interaction-existing-ru-final.log passes the unchanged tests/i18n-r2-ru-drive.mjs across 26 public routes plus a noindex 404 at widths 360 and 1280, including delayed module edits, late takeover edits, queued submit with animation frames deliberately suspended, eagerHash:false behavior, retries, keyboard, reduced-motion, chart-result and font checks. This run uses the existing inline-critical-styles.mjs postbuild output. Build/postbuild commands and failures are in interaction-check-commands.json. No stylesheet or route policy source changed.

The author inspected the actual Russian mobile action capture: the existing action styling is retained, the localized privacy note is visible, and the keyboard-focused download control is operable. Generated screenshots are synthetic fixtures, not user birth records.

## Failures and counterexamples preserved

- Initial source assertions exposed a hardcoded locale-key count; parity remained enforced after updating it. A focused TypeScript test-spy signature was corrected. An initial wrong Astro executable path produced MODULE_NOT_FOUND; corrected invocation and raw logs remain.
- Receipt Freeze 1 was rejected. Current imported fixed-offset zones succeed in old charts but fail the existing receipt zone grammar. Sixteen historical subminute transitions likewise succeed in old charts but cannot truthfully satisfy the local-resolution codec because the current resolver omitted dst-gap. Exact signed-zone and subminute reproductions, Freeze 1 source/identity, corrected focused tests and independent fixtures remain. Known-time exact-pole coverage is also explicitly preserved without a receipt. These are intentional pre-natal availability fallbacks, not silently altered receipts.
- The first author browser selector matched a native option instead of a place-list option; the corrected harness scopes that selector. The next run passed five locale downloads and the fresh-calculation group before the Russian product failure. RU DOM and CDP hook diagnostics proved untouched SSR date/time/default house replay caused input revision to advance after shared initialization; the existing receipt fence correctly refused the old result’s receipt.
- The old interaction directive fails three of the initial 12 native controls. The first dirty-replay draft passed 14 controls but independent reviewer Chrome probes demonstrated that restoring selected indexes changes the value when hydration reorders options. The draft is retained as interaction-index-draft.ts; the correction uses selected values and passes 16 author and two independent reorder controls.
- The first unchanged RU-drive invocation on raw Astro output stopped because its mandatory postbuild deferred stylesheets had not yet been declared. The existing unchanged stylesheet postbuild was then run, and the exact original test passed. Both failure and correction are retained; the test expectation was not weakened.
- The pre-existing bundle gate reports two structural assumptions: an inert receipt enum string is mistaken for an astronomy-engine import, and full-engine marker checks assume all static code remains in the entry file despite the delivered shared adapter chunk. The raw failure is retained. Root owns a separate correction measuring the whole static closure under the unchanged budget and adversarial negative fixtures. The author did not report this gate as passed or modify it.

